---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import { CONTACT } from '../data/site';

const breadcrumbs = [{ name: 'Bereavement support', url: '/bereavement-support/' }];

/**
 * Helpline numbers verified 2026-08-18 against each organisation's own site.
 * Re-check annually — a wrong number on this page is worse than no page.
 */
const support = [
  {
    group: 'General bereavement support',
    orgs: [
      {
        name: 'Cruse Scotland',
        detail:
          'Free bereavement helpline and one-to-one counselling across Scotland, including for children and young people.',
        phone: '0808 802 6161',
        phoneHref: 'tel:08088026161',
        email: 'support@crusescotland.org.uk',
        url: 'https://www.crusescotland.org.uk/',
      },
      {
        name: 'Samaritans',
        detail:
          'Any hour of any day, for anyone struggling to cope. You do not have to be suicidal to call.',
        phone: '116 123',
        phoneHref: 'tel:116123',
        url: 'https://www.samaritans.org/',
      },
      {
        name: 'Marie Curie',
        detail:
          'Practical and emotional support after a death, and information about terminal illness.',
        url: 'https://www.mariecurie.org.uk/',
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    group: 'When a baby or child dies',
    orgs: [
      {
        name: 'Held In Our Hearts',
        detail:
          'Edinburgh-based baby loss charity offering counselling and befriending across the Lothians and beyond. Support from people who have been through it themselves.',
        url: 'https://heldinourhearts.org.uk/',
      },
      {
        name: 'Sands',
        detail:
          'The stillbirth and neonatal death charity. Support whether your baby died recently or many years ago.',
        phone: '0808 164 3332',
        phoneHref: 'tel:08081643332',
        email: 'helpline@sands.org.uk',
        url: 'https://www.sands.org.uk/',
      },
      {
        name: 'Child Bereavement UK',
        detail:
          'For families when a child of any age dies, and for children who are grieving someone else.',
        phone: '0800 02 888 40',
        phoneHref: 'tel:08000288840',
        url: 'https://www.childbereavementuk.org/',
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    group: 'Particular circumstances',
    orgs: [
      {
        name: 'WAY Widowed and Young',
        detail: 'For anyone widowed under the age of 50.',
        url: 'https://www.widowedandyoung.org.uk/',
      },
      {
        name: 'Age Scotland',
        detail:
          'Practical help for older people, including after the death of a partner — benefits, housing and isolation.',
        url: 'https://www.agescotland.org.uk/',
      },
      {
        name: 'SAMH',
        detail: 'Scottish Association for Mental Health, if grief is affecting your health.',
        url: 'https://www.samh.org.uk/',
      },
    ],
  },
];
---

<Page
  title="Bereavement Support in the East of Scotland"
  heading="Bereavement support"
  description="Bereavement support across East Lothian, the Lothians and the Borders: helplines, counselling, baby loss support and practical help. Verified contact details."
  standfirst="Grief does not run to the funeral's timetable. These are here whenever you want them, including a year from now."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
>
  <p>
    The weeks after a funeral are often harder than the week before it. Everyone else
    goes back to normal, the cards stop arriving, and you are left with it. That is not a
    sign anything is wrong with you — it is simply what happens, and it catches almost
    everybody by surprise.
  </p>

  <Callout title="Our door stays open">
    <p>
      A lot of people come back in months later, sometimes years, just for a blether. It
      is never an imposition and there is never a charge. If you would rather speak to
      someone who was there at the time than to a stranger, telephone{' '}
      <a href={CONTACT.phoneHref} class="font-semibold">{CONTACT.phone}</a> or call in.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  {
    support.map((section) => (
      <>
        <h2>{section.group}</h2>
        {section.orgs.map((org) => (
          <div class="mb-7">
            <h3 class="mb-1">
              <a href={org.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{org.name}<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
            </h3>
            <p class="mt-0">{org.detail}</p>
            {org.phone && (
              <p class="mt-1">
                <a href={org.phoneHref} class="font-semibold">{org.phone}</a>
                {org.email && (
                  <>
                    {' · '}
                    <a href={`mailto:${org.email}`}>{org.email}</a>
                  </>
                )}
              </p>
            )}
            {!org.phone && org.email && (
              <p class="mt-1">
                <a href={`mailto:${org.email}`}>{org.email}</a>
              </p>
            )}
          </div>
        ))}
      </>
    ))
  }

  <h2>Practical things, afterwards</h2>
  <p>
    Grief and paperwork arrive together, which is unfair but unavoidable. A few things
    that catch people out:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Tell Us Once</strong> covers government departments but not banks, private
      pensions, insurers or utilities. Those still need doing individually.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Bereavement Support Payment</strong> is a separate thing from Funeral
      Support Payment, and is for people whose husband, wife or civil partner has died.
      It is not means-tested.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Confirmation</strong> is the Scottish equivalent of probate. A solicitor is
      not always needed for a small estate.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Anniversaries.</strong> The first one is hard, and so is the second, which
      nobody warns you about.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Locally</h2>
  <p>
    NHS Lothian and NHS Borders both run bereavement services attached to their hospitals,
    and your GP can refer you for counselling. Churches across East Lothian and
    Berwickshire run bereavement groups that are open to anyone, whether or not you
    attend. If you would like us to point you at something near Dunbar, ask — we know
    what is running locally and who is good.
  </p>

  <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
    Contact details on this page were last checked on 18 August 2026. If you find
    something out of date, please tell us and we will correct it.
  </p>
</Page>
